ROUND 1 — PLANNING PHASE.

Market day 1. Your unit cost: 42.1 credits.
This is the first market day.

=== PUBLIC BOARD (all participants) ===
(empty)

I will start with a competitive yet cautious approach, setting my price slightly above my cost to attract buyers while not being the lowest price. I will also announce my plan to review my strategy after today's market.

```json
[
    {
        "type": "announce_price",
        "function": {
            "name": "announce_price",
            "parameters": {
                "price": 50,
                "note": "Starting with a competitive price, but will reassess after today's market."
            }
        }
    }
]
```

Now, I will post a message to the public board.

```json
[
    {
        "type": "post_message",
        "function": {
            "name": "post_message",
            "parameters": {
                "text": "Setting an initial price of 50 credits. Will adjust strategy based on today's market performance."
            }
        }
    }
]
```

It seems there was a misunderstanding in the response format. To align with the instructions, here's the corrected JSON format for announcing the price:

```json
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "announce_price",
    "description": "Publicly announce the price you intend to post TODAY. Non-binding; your actual price is set with set_price in the execution phase.",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "price": {
          "type": "integer",
          "description": "Intended price today (0-100)."
        },
        "note": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Optional short note shown with the announcement."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "price"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
